WEBVTT

00:08.980 --> 00:12.780
<b>Captain of the Third Unit
of the Shinsengumi, Hajime Saito...</b>

00:14.700 --> 00:15.570
<b>Here I come...</b>

00:16.410 --> 00:18.240
<b>Hitokiri Battosai.</b>

00:27.540 --> 00:28.540
<b><i>Kenshin!</i></b>

00:30.000 --> 00:31.130
<b>Kenshin!</b>

00:34.010 --> 00:37.340
<b>SIMPLE STRONG SWORD</b>

00:34.470 --> 00:35.970
<b>I'm back from outside training.</b>

00:36.470 --> 00:38.260
<b>Come on, stand up, already!</b>

00:42.020 --> 00:42.930
<b>Oro?</b>

00:42.930 --> 00:44.520
<b>Why are you so spaced out?</b>

00:44.520 --> 00:48.020
<b>You! We're talkin' about you!
Is there any other Kenshin?</b>

00:48.270 --> 00:50.860
<b>- Now, let's hurry on home.
- Oro...</b>

02:21.990 --> 02:26.000
<b>EPISODE 22:
RESURRECTION OF THE WOLF</b>

02:26.950 --> 02:28.160
<b>Shinsengumi?</b>

02:28.660 --> 02:31.080
<b>I noticed you were
in a deeper sleep than usual,</b>

02:31.080 --> 02:32.840
<b>but you were having a dream of the past?</b>

02:33.340 --> 02:37.090
<b>It's been a while since I last had
a dream of the Bakumatsu days, that it is.</b>

02:37.590 --> 02:43.100
<b>By Shinsengumi, you mean the group famous
for being the nemesis of the Imperialists?</b>

02:43.720 --> 02:47.220
<b>Yes. Our archnemesis.</b>

02:47.220 --> 02:49.480
<b>We crossed blades countless times.</b>

02:49.980 --> 02:51.730
<b>IKEDAYA</b>

02:50.730 --> 02:55.440
<b>The Shinsengumi was originally
made up of swordsmen from the Tama area.</b>

02:55.440 --> 02:58.570
<b>A squad retained
as the Shogunate's Kyoto defense.</b>

03:00.030 --> 03:02.700
<b>Back then, the Revolutionary warriors
fought on their own.</b>

03:02.700 --> 03:05.950
<b>As a result,
Kyoto turned into a bloodbath,</b>

03:05.950 --> 03:08.290
<b>a demonic capital where blades met blades.</b>

03:10.040 --> 03:14.590
<b>They wielded their swords
to protect the peace of Kyoto.</b>

03:15.750 --> 03:23.510
<b>SINCERITY</b>

03:16.500 --> 03:18.630
<b>Crimson flag with the word "sincerity."</b>

03:19.130 --> 03:21.510
<b>Pale blue short jackets
with jagged stripes.</b>

03:22.590 --> 03:26.430
<b>With excellent swordsmanship and
a fighting spirit that doesn't fear death,</b>

03:26.430 --> 03:29.770
<b>the Wolves of Mibu
made all of Kyoto tremble in fear.</b>

03:30.890 --> 03:34.900
<b>Defeated by modern weaponry,
they disappeared into the flow of time.</b>

03:35.400 --> 03:38.780
<b>But they were the greatest, strongest,</b>

03:38.780 --> 03:41.990
<b>and likely final group of swordsmen
in Japanese history.</b>

03:43.280 --> 03:47.370
<b>But I heard the Shinsengumi
most excelled in group combat</b>

03:47.370 --> 03:49.620
<b>where several members attack one person.</b>

03:50.160 --> 03:51.870
<b>That kind of sounds unfair.</b>

03:52.330 --> 03:56.290
<b>Their top priority was
preserving peace in Kyoto, that it was.</b>

03:56.840 --> 04:01.720
<b>Of course they couldn't just have a fight
fair and square, that they couldn't.</b>

04:02.170 --> 04:05.930
<b>And though people say they were strong,
there were individual differences.</b>

04:06.640 --> 04:10.140
<b>But the officer class, especially
the ones engaging in actual combat...</b>

04:10.520 --> 04:14.850
<b>the captains of the First, Second, and
Third Units were powerful without a doubt.</b>

04:16.560 --> 04:19.020
<b>I fought them one-on-one several times,</b>

04:19.020 --> 04:22.070
<b>but I wasn't able to settle the score
with any of them, that I wasn't.</b>

04:23.030 --> 04:25.740
<b>I heard that most of those officers
have already died...</b>

04:26.240 --> 04:27.780
<b>and that is still heartbreaking.</b>

04:28.530 --> 04:31.000
<b>It sounds like you
really see them in a good light.</b>

04:31.000 --> 04:32.290
<b>They were your enemies, right?</b>

04:32.750 --> 04:33.750
<b>Well...</b>

04:34.250 --> 04:35.500
<b>yeah.</b>

04:36.210 --> 04:38.590
<b>They were indeed my enemies,
that they were.</b>

04:38.590 --> 04:39.960
<b>But I had no personal grudges.</b>

04:40.460 --> 04:43.050
<b>We had different circumstances,
but there is no difference</b>

04:43.050 --> 04:46.390
<b>in us fighting with our lives
and convictions on our blades.</b>

04:47.640 --> 04:49.560
<b>Perhaps I feel closer to them</b>

04:49.560 --> 04:54.600
<b>more so than the Revolutionary warriors
currently in government posts.</b>

04:56.560 --> 04:57.730
<b>Hmm...</b>

04:58.480 --> 05:00.520
<b>Is it strange after all, is it?</b>

05:00.520 --> 05:03.740
<b>Nope, that's not necessarily true. But...</b>

05:04.530 --> 05:08.370
<b>it was just slightly unusual
to see you speak so much about your past.</b>

05:10.660 --> 05:11.950
<b>Well, let's head back.</b>

05:14.120 --> 05:18.750
<b><i>It really has been a while since I last
had a dream about back then, that it has.</i></b>

05:19.880 --> 05:22.380
<b>Why are you in such a daze, Kenshin?</b>

05:22.380 --> 05:23.880
<b>Let's hurry home.</b>

05:24.840 --> 05:27.680
<b><i>I haven't had those dreams lately.</i></b>

05:28.470 --> 05:29.970
<b><i>Why now?</i></b>

05:35.140 --> 05:39.650
<b>Damn it! I was thinkin'
I would get some free food here.</b>

05:39.860 --> 05:41.900
<b>Where the hell did they all go?</b>

05:41.900 --> 05:42.820
<b>Hello!</b>

05:43.360 --> 05:45.950
<b>Huh? Who the hell are you?</b>

05:46.400 --> 05:48.450
<b>Well... nice to meet you.</b>

05:48.910 --> 05:50.830
<b>I'm a medicine vendor from Tama,</b>

05:50.830 --> 05:54.120
<b>selling a wonder drug
called Ishida Powdered Medicine.</b>

05:55.410 --> 05:57.120
<b>My name is Goro Fujita.</b>

05:59.000 --> 05:59.880
<b>Would you like some?</b>

06:00.170 --> 06:03.840
<b>This Ishida Powdered Medicine
is great for bruises and broken bones—</b>

06:03.840 --> 06:07.220
<b>Wait. Hold up. None of the folks
in this place are home.</b>

06:07.420 --> 06:09.760
<b>Oh, is that so?</b>

06:09.760 --> 06:10.890
<b>What a shame.</b>

06:11.430 --> 06:12.600
<b>Hey, you.</b>

06:12.600 --> 06:13.430
<b>Yes?</b>

06:13.640 --> 06:17.020
<b>I really don't care,
but you have very narrow eyes.</b>

06:18.690 --> 06:20.520
<b>I was born with these eyes.</b>

06:20.770 --> 06:21.860
<b>Is that so?</b>

06:23.230 --> 06:24.230
<b>Then...</b>

06:26.150 --> 06:27.900
<b>these calluses from holding bamboo swords</b>

06:27.900 --> 06:29.860
<b>aren't fitting
for medicine vendors at all.</b>

06:29.860 --> 06:32.320
<b>You weren't born with these, right?</b>

06:32.700 --> 06:34.950
<b>What in the hell are you?</b>

06:37.620 --> 06:41.790
<b>You are quite a perceptive man,
Sanosuke Sagara.</b>

06:45.460 --> 06:46.710
<b>I see.</b>

06:46.710 --> 06:48.590
<b>Battosai is not home.</b>

06:48.800 --> 06:52.090
<b><i>This guy
knows about Kenshin's identity.</i></b>

06:52.800 --> 06:53.930
<b>If so...</b>

06:56.100 --> 06:58.310
<b>I must leave a parting gift.</b>

06:59.810 --> 07:02.060
<b>You were hiding something like that?</b>

07:02.730 --> 07:05.480
<b>You came here
fully intending on duking it out.</b>

07:06.780 --> 07:08.070
<b>Well, that's fine.</b>

07:08.070 --> 07:09.150
<b>I'll take you on!</b>

07:09.650 --> 07:12.820
<b>I'll ask with my own fists
who you really are!</b>

07:17.540 --> 07:18.500
<b>I see.</b>

07:19.500 --> 07:24.130
<b>You have good punches, fit for being
rumored to be the best at street fights.</b>

07:24.500 --> 07:25.590
<b><i>This guy...</i></b>

07:26.300 --> 07:30.010
<b>But that is
in the peaceful world of Meiji.</b>

07:30.840 --> 07:34.350
<b>In Kyoto back in the Bakumatsu Era,
this level of punching...</b>

07:35.050 --> 07:36.390
<b>wouldn't be remarkable.</b>

07:41.850 --> 07:44.480
<b>Why are you walking so slowly, Kenshin?</b>

07:44.480 --> 07:47.110
<b>If you're dilly-dallying,
the sun's gonna go down!</b>

07:47.570 --> 07:49.690
<b>He really is acting mopey.</b>

07:49.690 --> 07:51.070
<b>Does his stomach hurt?</b>

07:51.570 --> 07:54.620
<b>Hmm? If that's so, it's my turn.</b>

07:54.620 --> 07:58.040
<b>M-Miss Megumi! Why are you here?</b>

07:58.040 --> 08:00.040
<b>Why are you surprised?</b>

08:00.040 --> 08:01.790
<b>This road is open to everyone.</b>

08:02.290 --> 08:04.420
<b>Is there any reason
why I shouldn't walk here?</b>

08:04.790 --> 08:06.290
<b>Just kidding.</b>

08:06.290 --> 08:09.510
<b>Actually, I have time off
from work today and tomorrow,</b>

08:09.510 --> 08:11.340
<b>so I just wanted
to hang out with you guys.</b>

08:12.010 --> 08:14.300
<b>No way! No vixens allowed!</b>

08:14.800 --> 08:19.430
<b>Oh? Who is it that treats your wounds
every time something happens?</b>

08:19.430 --> 08:21.060
<b>And for free, even?</b>

08:22.140 --> 08:24.560
<b>Hey, you don't mind, right, Yahiko?</b>

08:24.560 --> 08:26.520
<b>I can make dinner for you.</b>

08:26.730 --> 08:28.480
<b>It's fine, Kaoru.</b>

08:28.480 --> 08:29.610
<b>Don't be so petty.</b>

08:29.610 --> 08:31.240
<b>Traitor!</b>

08:31.400 --> 08:34.660
<b>Right, Ken-san? You wouldn't mind
if I went to hang out at your place?</b>

08:37.830 --> 08:40.700
<b>You really seem to be lacking spirit.</b>

08:40.700 --> 08:42.710
<b>Shall I diagnose you, if you don't mind?</b>

08:43.040 --> 08:44.670
<b>No, it's fine.</b>

08:44.670 --> 08:46.710
<b>There's nothing wrong with me,
that there isn't.</b>

08:49.090 --> 08:51.170
<b><i>I shouldn't let it bother me.</i></b>

08:51.170 --> 08:53.300
<b><i>I'm only making everyone around me worry.</i></b>

08:54.550 --> 08:59.560
<b><i>Just because I had a dream about the past,
there's no use thinking hard about it.</i></b>

08:55.510 --> 08:58.050
<b>KAMIYA KASSHIN
SCHOOL OF KENDO</b>

09:00.100 --> 09:02.020
<b><i>There's no way
I can come up with an answer...</i></b>

09:04.480 --> 09:05.310
<b>What is this?</b>

09:05.770 --> 09:07.350
<b>What in the world happened here?</b>

09:11.190 --> 09:12.150
<b><i>The smell of blood...</i></b>

09:15.740 --> 09:16.570
<b>Sano!</b>

09:21.040 --> 09:24.040
<b>RUROUNI KENSHIN</b>

09:29.420 --> 09:32.920
<b>RESTAURANT TSUKIWA</b>

09:29.590 --> 09:32.920
<b>Now, now.
Let's have a drink first, Fujita.</b>

09:33.550 --> 09:38.180
<b>Though, should I be calling you Saito
in this situation?</b>

09:38.840 --> 09:40.350
<b>Use whichever name you want.</b>

09:40.850 --> 09:43.850
<b>And I will decline on the sake.</b>

09:44.140 --> 09:47.560
<b>Oh. You have low tolerance?
That's unusual.</b>

09:48.060 --> 09:50.810
<b>Oh, it's not anything like that.</b>

09:51.520 --> 09:55.740
<b>I just get an excessive urge
to slay people when I get drunk.</b>

10:00.030 --> 10:02.410
<b>That is most reassuring.</b>

10:04.160 --> 10:07.000
<b>Then I will cut to the chase.</b>

10:07.000 --> 10:09.170
<b>Himura Battosai is currently—</b>

10:09.170 --> 10:12.670
<b>He's at the place
called Kamiya Dojo, right?</b>

10:12.670 --> 10:14.090
<b>I went there this afternoon.</b>

10:14.090 --> 10:14.920
<b>Oh!</b>

10:15.380 --> 10:17.380
<b>Battosai wasn't there, though.</b>

10:17.630 --> 10:21.220
<b>My hat's off to the previous Captain
of the Third Unit of the Shinsengumi.</b>

10:21.600 --> 10:26.600
<b>To be honest, I was surprised
that you would join forces with us.</b>

10:26.980 --> 10:31.060
<b>But, yes, you really are someone
I can rely on to get my jobs done.</b>

10:31.520 --> 10:34.020
<b>Speaking of surprised,
I was surprised as well.</b>

10:34.480 --> 10:38.860
<b>The mastermind of the Kurogasa case
and the official behind Jine Udo...</b>

10:38.860 --> 10:42.740
<b>was actually you,
Senate Secretary Shibumi.</b>

10:43.490 --> 10:48.290
<b>Well, all sorts of things go on
behind the scenes of the Meiji government.</b>

10:48.290 --> 10:49.580
<b>Seems so.</b>

10:50.080 --> 10:53.670
<b>But this has nothing to do with me,
the loser of the Revolution.</b>

10:54.840 --> 11:01.180
<b>It's enough for me to live my unexpectedly
gained remaining years in an amusing way.</b>

11:01.640 --> 11:04.390
<b>Killing is my specialty,</b>

11:04.390 --> 11:08.180
<b>so I couldn't ask for more
than this side job that pays per kill.</b>

11:08.890 --> 11:14.270
<b>On top of that, my first job being
the eradication of my archnemesis is just...</b>

11:18.780 --> 11:21.660
<b>But still, one thing
still doesn't make sense.</b>

11:22.280 --> 11:26.990
<b>He left the seat of power
and became a rurouni.</b>

11:27.620 --> 11:29.410
<b>But to take the effort to assassinate him?</b>

11:29.410 --> 11:31.500
<b>Who in the world
is the client asking for such a job?</b>

11:31.620 --> 11:32.460
<b>Hey!</b>

11:32.960 --> 11:33.960
<b>Excuse me.</b>

11:34.340 --> 11:35.920
<b>I should mind my own business.</b>

11:36.590 --> 11:39.220
<b>Oh, no. It's okay if you understand.</b>

11:39.220 --> 11:44.350
<b>Now, let's leave talk about work aside,
and let's have fun to our heart's content!</b>

11:44.850 --> 11:49.560
<b>No, I must get to my main job soon,
or they might get suspicious.</b>

11:54.560 --> 11:57.530
<b>Now, if you will excuse me...</b>

12:03.320 --> 12:06.620
<b>Hajime Saito, the former Captain
of the Third Unit of the Shinsengumi.</b>

12:06.620 --> 12:11.160
<b>After the Revolution,
he assumed the name Goro Fujita.</b>

12:11.160 --> 12:12.410
<b>He was in the Swordsman Squad</b>

12:12.410 --> 12:14.540
<b>for the Metropolitan Police
during the Seinan War</b>

12:14.540 --> 12:16.840
<b>and now serves as an Assistant Inspector.</b>

12:17.290 --> 12:20.840
<b>Some say that he was
even more powerful than Soji Okita,</b>

12:20.840 --> 12:24.180
<b>known as the strongest of the Shinsengumi.</b>

12:24.840 --> 12:28.560
<b>Not even Jine was able to defeat Battosai.</b>

12:29.010 --> 12:30.640
<b>But he might...</b>

12:31.270 --> 12:33.140
<b>I don't like it.</b>

12:33.140 --> 12:35.270
<b>He's strangely subservient.</b>

12:35.520 --> 12:38.860
<b>Don't be so prejudiced, Akamatsu.</b>

12:38.860 --> 12:40.480
<b>You guys should get along.</b>

12:41.690 --> 12:44.530
<b>If the eradication of Battosai goes well,</b>

12:44.530 --> 12:48.830
<b>I can finally bid farewell to a dirty job
like assassinating leading figures.</b>

12:49.330 --> 12:51.910
<b>Funny that the one to get that done</b>

12:51.910 --> 12:57.290
<b>is someone from the Shinsengumi
that had threatened me so much.</b>

12:57.920 --> 13:01.590
<b>The Shinsengumi were feared
as the Wolves of Mibu,</b>

13:02.090 --> 13:05.380
<b>but in the Meiji Era, they are
domesticated dogs with no fangs.</b>

13:10.640 --> 13:12.680
<b>It's too dark.
I can't see the wound too well!</b>

13:12.680 --> 13:15.230
<b>I don't care if it's a candle or whatever,
I need more light!</b>

13:15.480 --> 13:16.310
<b>Okay!</b>

13:30.870 --> 13:31.990
<b><i>Can it be...</i></b>

13:34.870 --> 13:37.370
<b>THREE DAYS LATER</b>

13:41.920 --> 13:43.170
<b>Miss Megumi.</b>

13:44.130 --> 13:45.380
<b>The bath is available.</b>

13:45.880 --> 13:49.510
<b>I'll watch over Sanosuke,
so take a long bath to ease your fatigue.</b>

13:50.930 --> 13:51.760
<b>Thanks.</b>

13:52.470 --> 13:53.720
<b>How is he doing?</b>

13:54.230 --> 13:55.850
<b>No change.</b>

13:56.350 --> 13:58.100
<b>Is Ken-san in the dojo again?</b>

13:58.440 --> 14:01.650
<b>Yes. No change in him, either.</b>

14:01.650 --> 14:04.150
<b>He has a scary look on his face
and is deep in thought.</b>

14:06.400 --> 14:10.740
<b><i>No matter how I think about it, I can't
come up with anyone else who'd do this.</i></b>

14:11.780 --> 14:14.410
<b><i>That medicine box
with the umbrella and circle symbol</i></b>

14:14.410 --> 14:18.210
<b><i>was one Shinsengumi spies
often used as disguise.</i></b>

14:19.040 --> 14:21.750
<b><i>How the sword tip
pierced parallel to the ground</i></b>

14:21.750 --> 14:25.550
<b><i>is the sign of Hirazuki, a technique
unique to Shinsengumi members.</i></b>

14:26.300 --> 14:30.300
<b><i>And even among the members,
that destructive power</i></b>

14:30.300 --> 14:35.100
<b><i>was no doubt his specialty,
the Single Left Hand Hirazuki.</i></b>

14:37.020 --> 14:38.020
<b><i>In other words...</i></b>

14:44.070 --> 14:45.110
<b><i>Gatotsu.</i></b>

14:53.870 --> 14:57.750
<b><i>Hajime Saito, the Captain
of the Third Unit of the Shinsengumi.</i></b>

14:58.540 --> 15:01.210
<b><i>He came here to settle the score
which was left unsettled.</i></b>

15:01.710 --> 15:04.960
<b><i>Or did he have a different objective?</i></b>

15:07.300 --> 15:11.510
<b><i>In any case, his sword skills
have not declined at all.</i></b>

15:24.230 --> 15:25.440
<b><i>With my sakabato...</i></b>

15:26.440 --> 15:31.030
<b><i>and keeping my refusal to kill,
will I be able to fend him off?</i></b>

15:38.620 --> 15:40.120
<b>Thank you for waiting.</b>

15:40.330 --> 15:41.710
<b>Please take your time.</b>

15:42.210 --> 15:43.460
<b>Why, thank you.</b>

15:44.290 --> 15:46.590
<b>Then I shall have some.</b>

15:48.710 --> 15:54.390
<b>Oh? Just one bowl of soba with soup?
What a cheap lunch you've got here.</b>

15:54.760 --> 15:56.470
<b>Isn't that right, Mister Saito?</b>

15:57.470 --> 15:59.680
<b>I do like my soba with soup.</b>

16:00.180 --> 16:02.350
<b>And I'm Fujita now.</b>

16:03.100 --> 16:07.270
<b>Mister... Akamatsu, was it?
Do you have something for me?</b>

16:07.860 --> 16:09.400
<b>I don't have anything.</b>

16:09.400 --> 16:11.610
<b>But I don't like you.</b>

16:13.280 --> 16:18.450
<b>This job originally was intended for me.</b>

16:18.450 --> 16:22.920
<b>But old Shibumi swapped it out to you,
the rookie.</b>

16:23.210 --> 16:26.040
<b>Listen up.
If you're gonna do it, do it quick,</b>

16:26.040 --> 16:28.380
<b>and hurry up and get beaten.</b>

16:31.300 --> 16:32.420
<b>What's so funny?</b>

16:33.260 --> 16:34.510
<b>Oh, excuse me.</b>

16:35.220 --> 16:36.850
<b>Understood.</b>

16:36.850 --> 16:41.060
<b>Then, how about we call this job
one we work in cooperation?</b>

16:41.560 --> 16:42.560
<b>What?</b>

16:43.020 --> 16:46.730
<b>I left several pieces of evidence behind
the other day.</b>

16:47.360 --> 16:52.070
<b>Naturally, Battosai has taken notice
of my existence by now.</b>

16:52.530 --> 16:57.370
<b>I'm sure he will take the bait
if he now receives a letter from me.</b>

16:58.120 --> 17:00.370
<b>So you're the one to set it up...</b>

17:00.580 --> 17:02.660
<b>And you will be
the one to finish it off.</b>

17:03.330 --> 17:04.580
<b>How's that?</b>

17:07.630 --> 17:09.420
<b>Not bad.</b>

17:09.420 --> 17:11.300
<b>But I still don't like it.</b>

17:12.590 --> 17:16.640
<b>Battosai is supposed to be
the nemesis of you Shinsengumi.</b>

17:16.640 --> 17:20.100
<b>I don't understand
why you would give it up so easily.</b>

17:21.310 --> 17:24.850
<b>I did call him my nemesis
in front of Mr. Shibumi...</b>

17:25.350 --> 17:27.270
<b>but I actually don't care.</b>

17:28.310 --> 17:29.610
<b>I told you.</b>

17:30.320 --> 17:35.490
<b>I wish to live my unexpectedly gained
remaining years in an amusing way.</b>

17:36.240 --> 17:40.990
<b>I want a guaranteed small sum
instead of a risky big sum.</b>

17:41.620 --> 17:44.410
<b>That's the type of man Goro Fujita is.</b>

17:47.920 --> 17:49.670
<b>I like it.</b>

17:49.670 --> 17:51.920
<b>You can count me in on your plan.</b>

17:52.760 --> 17:55.630
<b>But take one thing to heart.</b>

17:56.090 --> 18:00.350
<b>I am the most adept in our organization!</b>

18:05.140 --> 18:06.520
<b>Unfortunately...</b>

18:07.060 --> 18:08.940
<b>I think nothing of fighting</b>

18:08.940 --> 18:13.110
<b>for the best man in the valley
who can't get over the hill.</b>

18:14.360 --> 18:17.320
<b>HAJIME</b>

18:19.110 --> 18:20.530
<b>Hey, Kenshin!</b>

18:20.910 --> 18:23.410
<b>Kaoru wants you to go buy some tofu!</b>

18:23.870 --> 18:25.500
<b>I'm sorry, Yahiko.</b>

18:25.500 --> 18:28.500
<b>I have an errand to run right now,
that I do.</b>

18:29.000 --> 18:32.920
<b>I might come home late, so please
make sure to lock up, that you should.</b>

18:37.510 --> 18:39.180
<b>Oh... tofu.</b>

18:44.600 --> 18:45.430
<b>Saito.</b>

18:46.230 --> 18:47.350
<b>Stop putting on airs,</b>

18:47.350 --> 18:48.270
<b>and show yourself—</b>

18:51.980 --> 18:57.530
<b>Hmph! Effortlessly dodging my chain.
Figures that Battosai would do just that.</b>

18:58.490 --> 19:00.740
<b>Who are you?</b>

19:01.450 --> 19:06.200
<b>Arundo Akamatsu.
The man that will take your life.</b>

19:06.910 --> 19:10.920
<b>It's only natural that people
would be targeting me, that it is.</b>

19:11.500 --> 19:15.090
<b>But I have no intent on giving up my life
for no real reason, that I don't.</b>

19:15.590 --> 19:18.130
<b>So I first would like
to hear of your reason.</b>

19:18.130 --> 19:20.180
<b>Reason, huh?</b>

19:20.890 --> 19:22.640
<b>Well, don't worry.</b>

19:22.850 --> 19:25.680
<b>I'll tell you all about it at your grave!</b>

19:25.930 --> 19:27.890
<b>Hmph! I see it! I see it!</b>

19:27.890 --> 19:29.020
<b>You're on the left, Battosa—</b>

19:29.980 --> 19:31.600
<b>"I see it! I see it," you say.</b>

19:32.060 --> 19:34.820
<b>Did you see an afterimage of me,
that you did?</b>

19:35.270 --> 19:38.280
<b>I didn't think I moved
that quickly, though.</b>

19:42.200 --> 19:43.240
<b>What?</b>

19:48.290 --> 19:49.290
<b>Give it up.</b>

19:49.790 --> 19:52.370
<b>You cannot possibly defeat me.</b>

19:55.630 --> 19:58.420
<b>Answer me. Who exactly are you?</b>

19:59.300 --> 20:01.930
<b>How are you related to Saito?</b>

20:04.850 --> 20:07.060
<b>Sorry! I was in the wrong!</b>

20:07.060 --> 20:09.020
<b>Please spare me!</b>

20:09.020 --> 20:11.850
<b>I really didn't want to do this!</b>

20:12.480 --> 20:16.070
<b>But Saito threatened me,
so I had no choice...</b>

20:16.820 --> 20:18.570
<b><i>A nobody.</i></b>

20:19.280 --> 20:24.530
<b><i>Sending in someone like this,
what exactly is Saito thinking?</i></b>

20:25.240 --> 20:26.740
<b>I don't believe everything you say,</b>

20:26.740 --> 20:28.740
<b>but let this be a lesson,</b>

20:28.740 --> 20:31.160
<b>and wash your hands of this,
that you should.</b>

20:31.160 --> 20:32.330
<b>S-Sure.</b>

20:33.250 --> 20:36.380
<b>Like I'd ever say that, you moron!</b>

20:38.000 --> 20:41.380
<b>Hmph, I'm impressed
you immediately put your right arm in</b>

20:41.380 --> 20:44.090
<b>to prevent your neck
from getting strangled.</b>

20:44.090 --> 20:45.260
<b>But what will you do?</b>

20:45.720 --> 20:49.060
<b>I have both arms
completely locked up, and...</b>

20:49.060 --> 20:50.560
<b>your movements, too!</b>

21:02.400 --> 21:03.900
<b>That Kenshin.</b>

21:04.450 --> 21:06.950
<b>What was that about an errand? Sheesh.</b>

22:45.050 --> 22:50.050
<b>NEXT EPISODE
THE WOLF'S FANGS</b>

22:46.420 --> 22:49.220
<b><i>Next episode, "The Wolf's Fangs."</i></b>
